\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Soldiers of Christ, arise,
\par And put your armour on,
\par Strong in the stength which God supplies
\par Through His eternal Son;
\par Strong in the Lord of Hosts,
\par And in His mighty power,
\par Who in the strength of Jesus trusts
\par Is more than conqueror.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Stand then in His great might,
\par With all His strength endued;
\par But take, to arm you for the fight,
\par The panoply of God;
\par That, having all things done,
\par And all your conflicts passed,
\par Ye may o'ercome through Christ alone,
\par And stand entire at last.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Stand then against your foes,
\par In close and firmm array;
\par Legions of willy fiends oppose
\par Throughout the evil day:
\par But meek the sons of night;
\par But mock their vain design,
\par Armed in the arms of heavenly light,
\par Of righteousness divine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Leave no unguarded place,
\par No weakness of the soul;
\par Take every virtue, every grace,
\par And fortify the whole:
\par Indissolubly joined,
\par To battle all proceed;
\par But arm yourselves with all the mind
\par That was in Christ, your Head.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

